# ISO 27001 Learning Portfolio

This repository is part of my cybersecurity and GRC learning journey.  
It shows my **beginner-level understanding** of ISO/IEC 27001 and how the standard is used to manage information security risks in an organization.

I created this portfolio to practice turning ISO 27001 concepts into real documents such as risk registers, policies, and control mappings.

## What This Repository Includes

This repository includes simple examples of:
- An organizational security context
- A basic risk assessment and risk register
- A beginner-friendly Statement of Applicability (SOA)
- Sample security policies
- High-level control mappings
- Audit and improvement checklists

These examples are for learning and demonstration purposes.

## Why I Built This

I am pursuing a career in Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) within the cybersecurity field.  
This repository helps me:
- Practice applying security frameworks
- Build hands-on experience with ISO 27001
- Create a portfolio I can continue improving over time
